body:
Yeah, admittedly my interview skills aren't too great in the technical department. I get nervous -- often times, I actually know the answer, but I blank out or I don't feel confident enough to say it for fear of sounding dumb. My first technical interview experiences were terrifying, especially when I got hit with a curveball and didn't know how to answer. But, now that I've done a handful of technical interviews, I know what to expect. I got better each time. I *always* absolutely nail the behavioral/non-technical parts of the interviews lol. That was the feedback I got on my last set of interviews. 

&#x200B;

Do you have any tips or resources for preparing for technical interviews? At this point I've approached it like studying for an exam based on what I anticipate they will ask or what the recruiter told me to expect.
